{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>YHWH has reigned; He has donned grandeur.</b> — Since the way of kings is to don royal garments, they said by way of metaphor that HaShem 'donned grandeur.' It is a past-tense verb like אהב. When HaShem put on might, He girded Himself like one who girds himself to show his strength. The word עז serves together with לבש and with the word התאזר." "And the meaning of 'also the world is established' — that through the grandeur and power of HaShem it stands within the great sphere, like a point within a circle, and will not be shaken."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 93, :notes {0 "Read לבש as the lemma (from the verse); it functions both as the lemma-head and within Ibn Ezra's grammatical argument."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:07.619417376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}